Z||000000||Zorba||10-18-2000||12:00 PM||||Guys, I am trying to decide on a electric water pump for a v8 conversion. Can you recommend the best one for STREET use?<BR>I wanted to buy the V8 archie w/p drive system but I am unsure on how to go about the welding part of the set up. I don't have  access to a MIG WELDER and can't rent one locally and that's the only reason to go with an electric w/p. Am I missing something?<BR>IF the welding part is easy, I could care less about having the wp drive belt in the wheel well! Thanks for any suggestions.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Zorba||10-18-2000||12:11 PM|||| O.K. my brain is fried. I went to archie's site and it CLEARLY says:<BR>"At final assembly, in the car, the excess shaft length will be trimmed off and the lower pulley will be welded to the shaft. After these factors have been determined, you can remove the W/P rive assy..."<P>I guess, I can mark the position of the lower pulley once the belts are aligned  and take the shaft and pulley to a shop to have it welded in place. <P>I was confused because I thought that the shaft itself had to be welded to the harmonic balancer which is already installed in the car! Duh!||||reg||1
